cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PsyStat in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "PsyStat: A Comprehensive Statistical Analysis Tool for Psychology and Social Science Research"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2025-07-30
authors:
  - family-names: Setiawan
    given-names: Tery
    affiliation: "Universitas Kristen Maranatha & Radboud University"
abstract: >
  PsyStat is a modern, graphical desktop application designed for psychologists,
  social scientists, and researchers who require a powerful yet intuitive
  statistical analysis tool. It covers 17 analysis modules including data
  management, descriptives, t-tests, ANOVA (Type III SS with sphericity
  corrections), regression (OLS, logistic, multinomial), mediation analysis,
  EFA, CFA, SEM, CATPCA, latent profile analysis, psychometric network
  analysis, forecasting, and power analysis. All outputs are APA-formatted.
  PsyStat is distributed as a self-contained application for Windows and macOS.
keywords:
  - statistics
  - psychology
  - social science
  - SPSS alternative
  - factor analysis
  - structural equation modeling
  - ANOVA
  - regression
  - psychometrics
  - open source
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/terysetn02-source/psystat"
url: "https://github.com/terysetn02-source/psystat"
